WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.688
Here are the six workflow files, as
reviewed version one point oh bodies.

2
00:00:04.688 --> 00:00:05.938
Two are joiners.

3
00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:09.465
The pre-hire workflow runs
seven days before the hire date

4
00:00:09.465 --> 00:00:13.213
and generates the Temporary Access
Pass and sends it by email.

5
00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.805
The day-one workflow runs on the hire date

6
00:00:15.805 --> 00:00:18.625
and requests the
onboarding access package.

7
00:00:18.625 --> 00:00:21.727
One is the mover, triggered
by an attribute change:

8
00:00:21.727 --> 00:00:25.888
it notifies the manager and removes
an access package assignment.

9
00:00:25.888 --> 00:00:27.449
And three are leavers.

10
00:00:27.449 --> 00:00:32.314
On the leave date, employees are disabled,
their refresh tokens revoked and their

11
00:00:32.314 --> 00:00:37.250
package assignments removed; contractors
are disabled and their tokens revoked.

12
00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.261
Thirty days after the leave date,

13
00:00:39.261 --> 00:00:42.612
a separate post-separation
workflow deletes the user.

14
00:00:42.612 --> 00:00:43.900
Notice the scopes.

15
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:48.001
Every one reads the worker type
and a coded slot, never a name,

16
00:00:48.001 --> 00:00:51.910
so renaming an organization
can't silently drop anyone.
